The Attorney is authorised to do the following in the name of and on behalf of the Principal:
{{powers_granted}}
and, in connection with and only so far as is necessary for those acts:
(a) to sign, execute, and deliver any document, application, form, declaration, or acknowledgment;
(b) to appear before, and to make representations to, any public authority, office, court, or tribunal, and to sign and file any paper required by it;
(c) to receive and give valid receipts for any sum payable to the Principal;
(d) to correspond with any bank, authority, or person, and to obtain and give information;
(e) generally to do everything that is necessary and incidental to the acts expressly authorised above.
The authority in sub-clauses (a) to (e) is ancillary. It does not enlarge the acts expressly authorised, and shall be construed strictly by reference to them.

The Assignor represents and warrants to the Assignee that, as at the date of this Agreement:
(a) the Assignor is the sole and lawful owner of the intellectual property assigned, and is entitled to assign it;
(b) the intellectual property assigned is free of every mortgage, charge, lien, licence, and other encumbrance, and no person has any option or right of first refusal over it;
(c) the intellectual property assigned is original to the Assignor and does not, so far as the Assignor is aware, infringe the rights of any other person;
(d) no claim, proceeding, or opposition is pending or, so far as the Assignor is aware, threatened, in respect of the intellectual property assigned;
(e) where any of the intellectual property was made by an employee or a contractor of the Assignor, the Assignor has obtained a written assignment from that person sufficient to vest the rights in the Assignor;
(f) the Assignor has not previously assigned or exclusively licensed the intellectual property to any other person.
The Assignor shall indemnify the Assignee against loss arising from a breach of these warranties.
